{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA980007","title":"Free-living and particle associated microbial community dynamics in a free water surface constructed wetland","description":"The dataset contains 16S rRNA sequences of planktonic and sediment microbial community in a free water surface CW operating as a polishing step for secondary treated wastewater. The investigated constructed wetland was located in the South-West England. The study was carried out in summertime (July-September). Water and sediment samples were collected at different sampling points within the CW including inflow and outflow points as well as 2 internal sampling points. Water samples were filtered using 3um membranes to separate particle associated planktonic community and the filtrate was further filtered on 0.22um to capture free-living planktonic community. Sediment samples were collected at the same sampling points as water samples to observe association between sediment and planktonic community.","center":"University of Bath","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2023/06/05 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN35619136","MIMS Environmental/Metagenome sample from wastewater metagenome","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2021-07-14",2021,"GB","England",2656173,"Bath","probable",51.36,-2.27,"United Kingdom: Gloucestershire",null,"wastewater","secondary treated wastewater in constucted wetland","water sample","city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN35619137","MIMS Environmental/Metagenome sample from wastewater metagenome","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2021-07-14",2021,"GB","England",2656173,"Bath","probable",51.36,-2.27,"United Kingdom: Gloucestershire",null,"wastewater","secondary treated wastewater i